    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nFunctionality of organochlorosilanes in silicone synthesis.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nTrichlorosilanes have three functional chlorine atoms.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nHydrolysis yields trihydroxy silane RSi(OH)3, which condenses in three dimensions.\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Hydrolysis of alkyltrichlorosilane (RSiCl3) yields alkylsilanetriol RSi(OH)3.\n2. Because each molecule has three reactive silanol -OH groups, condensation polymerization occurs in three dimensions.\n3. This forms complex cross-linked polymeric silicone resins.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: RSiCl3\n\n6. WHY OTHER OPTIONS ARE WRONG:\nR2SiCl2 has functionality 2 and forms linear polymers; R3SiCl has functionality 1 and terminates chains.",
