      "stepByStep": "1. Hydrolysis of alkyltrichlorosilane (RSiCl3) yields alkylsilanetriol RSi(OH)3.\n2. Because each molecule has three reactive silanol -OH groups, condensation polymerization occurs in three dimensions.\n3. This forms complex cross-linked polymeric silicone resins.",
      "finalAnswer": "Option A: RSiCl3",
      "whyOtherOptionsWrong": "R2SiCl2 has functionality 2 and forms linear polymers; R3SiCl has functionality 1 and terminates chains."
